{"metadata":{"role":"collectionGroup","roleHeading":"API Collection","title":"Querying JSON","modules":[{"name":"LoomCore"}]},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/loomcore\/queryingjson"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/QueryingJSON","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Articles","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/IndexConventions","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/SafeInterpolation","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/ConcurrencyModel","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/FullTextSearch","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Articles"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"type":"heading","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SQLite ships a complete JSON toolkit — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_extract"},{"type":"text","text":", the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"->"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"->>"},{"type":"text","text":" operators, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_set"},{"type":"text","text":", aggregates, and the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_each"},{"type":"text","text":"\/"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_tree"},{"type":"text","text":" table-valued functions — and every OS version LoomCore supports includes it. This article shows the typed expression DSL over those functions. For how JSON gets "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"into"}]},{"type":"text","text":" a column in the first place, see "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/StoringCustomTypes"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The examples below assume a table of users whose "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"profile"},{"type":"text","text":" column holds a JSON document such as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"{\"displayName\":\"Alice\",\"age\":30,\"address\":{\"city\":\"Vienna\"},\"tags\":[\"swift\",\"sql\"]}"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"JSON-paths","text":"JSON paths"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every function that addresses part of a document takes a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONPath"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$"},{"type":"text","text":" is the document root, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$.address.city"},{"type":"text","text":" a nested member, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$.tags[0]"},{"type":"text","text":" an array element, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"$.\"key with spaces\""},{"type":"text","text":" a quoted key. Paths are usually written as string literals:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let profile = ColumnExpression<String>(\"profile\")","let city = profile.jsonValue(\"$.address.city\", as: String.self)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Paths render into the SQL as single-quoted literals, not bound parameters. This is deliberate: SQLite matches an expression index on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_extract(\"profile\", '$.age')"},{"type":"text","text":" only when the path is a literal token, so binding paths would silently turn indexed JSON lookups into table scans. The trade-offs are that a path is inlined like an identifier — treat it as trusted input, like a column name — and that statements differing only in their paths are distinct entries in the prepared-statement cache."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Extracting-values","text":"Extracting values"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Extraction states the expected Swift type up front, because a JSON node can decode to any storage class and LoomCore’s column reads are strictly checked:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let profile = ColumnExpression<String>(\"profile\")","","let age = profile.jsonValue(\"$.age\", as: Int.self)  \/\/ (\"profile\"->>'$.age')","let name = profile.jsonExtract(\"$.displayName\", as: String.self)  \/\/ JSON_EXTRACT(…)","","let adults = try await db.query(\"SELECT \\(name) FROM users WHERE \\(age >= 18)\") { stmt, _ in","  try String?.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Results are optional — a NULL document or a path that selects nothing yields NULL. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonValue(_:as:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"->>"},{"type":"text","text":" operator) returns plain SQL values; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonFragment(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"->"},{"type":"text","text":" operator) returns the selected node "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"as JSON text"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so string nodes keep their quotes and the result chains:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let profile = ColumnExpression<String>(\"profile\")","let city = profile.jsonFragment(\"$.address\").jsonValue(\"$.city\", as: String.self)"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Inspect documents with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonType(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (type name at a path), "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonValid()"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonArrayLength(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"; locate the syntax error in a broken document with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonErrorPosition()"},{"type":"text","text":" (SQLite 3.42+, iOS 17\/macOS 14)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Modifying-documents","text":"Modifying documents"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonSet(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" overwrites or creates, "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonInsert(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" only creates, and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonReplace(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" only overwrites. Each takes "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONAssignment"},{"type":"text","text":" pairs, and the choice of factory matters: SQLite treats a bound TEXT argument as a JSON "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"string"}]},{"type":"text","text":", so a nested document must be wrapped."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["struct Address: Codable, JSONBindable {","  let city: String","}","","let profile = ColumnExpression<String>(\"profile\")","try await db.exec(","  \"\"\"","  UPDATE users SET profile = \\(profile.jsonSet(","    .value(\"$.displayName\", \"Alice\"),","    .json(\"$.address\", Address(city: \"Vienna\"))","  ))","  \"\"\"",")"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":".value"},{"type":"text","text":" binds scalars — numbers, strings, booleans — directly; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".json"},{"type":"text","text":" wraps the bound text in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"JSON(?)"},{"type":"text","text":" so a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable"},{"type":"text","text":" nests as a real object rather than a string. Assigning a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" optional through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":".value"},{"type":"text","text":" stores JSON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Delete nodes with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonRemove(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and merge whole documents with "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonPatch(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" (RFC 7396: patch keys overwrite, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" removes). Unlike "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jsonSet"},{"type":"text","text":" values, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jsonPatch"},{"type":"text","text":" argument needs no wrapping — both sides are parsed as JSON, so passing a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable"},{"type":"text","text":" directly is exactly right."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Building-and-aggregating","text":"Building and aggregating"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/jsonArray(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/jsonObject(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":" construct documents in the SELECT list; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonGroupArray()"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/jsonGroupObject(name:value:)"},{"type":"text","text":" aggregate grouped rows. All four are non-optional: empty input yields "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'[]'"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"'{}'"},{"type":"text","text":", and NULL inputs become JSON "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"null"},{"type":"text","text":" members."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let author = ColumnExpression<String>(\"author\")","let title = ColumnExpression<String>(\"title\")","let shelves = try await db.query(","  \"SELECT \\(author), \\(title.jsonGroupArray()) FROM books GROUP BY \\(author)\"",") { stmt, _ in","  (try String.column(of: stmt, at: 0), try String.column(of: stmt, at: 1))","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The TEXT-is-a-string rule applies here too: to nest a column that already holds JSON, wrap it — "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jsonArray(tags.json())"},{"type":"text","text":", not "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jsonArray(tags)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"Iterating-with-JSONEACH-and-JSONTREE","text":"Iterating with JSON_EACH and JSON_TREE"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONEach"},{"type":"text","text":" yields one row per element of an array or object; "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONTree"},{"type":"text","text":" recurses into nested containers. Both are FROM-clause fragments — interpolate them after the tables and read rows through their typed column handles:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let userID = ColumnExpression<Int64>(\"id\", of: \"users\")","let profile = ColumnExpression<String>(\"profile\", of: \"users\")","let tag = JSONEach(profile, \"$.tags\")","","\/\/ Users tagged \"swift\" — one row per (user, tag) pair, filtered.","let swiftUsers = try await db.query(","  \"SELECT \\(userID) FROM users, \\(tag) WHERE \\(tag.value(as: String.self) == \"swift\")\"",") { stmt, _ in","  try Int64.column(of: stmt, at: 0)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"key"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"value"},{"type":"text","text":", and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"atom"},{"type":"text","text":" take "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"as:"},{"type":"text","text":" because their storage class varies per row (array keys are integers, object keys are strings); "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"type"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"fullkey"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"path"},{"type":"text","text":" — and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"parent"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONTree"},{"type":"text","text":" — are fixed. Two things to watch: qualify your own columns when names collide ("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"json_each"},{"type":"text","text":" exposes its own "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"id"},{"type":"text","text":"), and pass "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"alias:"},{"type":"text","text":" when the same function appears twice in one query."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"heading","level":3,"anchor":"JSONB","text":"JSONB"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"SQLite 3.45 added JSONB, a compact binary encoding that skips re-parsing on every access. It ships with iOS 18, macOS 15, macCatalyst 18, tvOS 18, watchOS 11, and visionOS 2, so the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jsonb"},{"type":"text","text":"-prefixed variants — "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonb()"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonbSet(_:_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/jsonbArray(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":", and friends — are annotated "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@available"},{"type":"text","text":" for those versions and return "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Data"},{"type":"text","text":" (BLOB) instead of "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"String"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let profile = ColumnExpression<String>(\"profile\")","if #available(iOS 18.0, macOS 15.0, macCatalyst 18.0, tvOS 18.0, watchOS 11.0, visionOS 2.0, *) {","  try await db.exec(\"UPDATE users SET profile = \\(profile.jsonb())\")","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every text-level function accepts JSONB input transparently on those OS versions, so a column can be migrated to JSONB without touching the queries that read it — with one exception: the one-argument "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonValid()","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" accepts only JSON text and reports JSONB as invalid. Validate migrated or mixed-storage columns with "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/Expression\/jsonValid(_:)","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", e.g. "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"data.jsonValid([.json, .jsonb])"},{"type":"text","text":". JSONB is an internal SQLite format: store it and query it, but do not parse the bytes outside SQLite. There is no "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"jsonb_each"},{"type":"text","text":" — "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONEach","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" already accepts JSONB input."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Extract, filter, modify, build, and iterate JSON documents with typed expressions over SQLite’s JSON functions."}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore"]]},"kind":"article","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONPath","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONBindable","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONExtract","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONAccessExpression","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONAssignment","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONModify","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONEach","doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONTree"],"anchor":"Topics"}],"references":{"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/TransactionsAndServices":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/transactionsandservices","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Transactions and Services","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/TransactionsAndServices","abstract":[{"text":"Atomic operations, savepoint nesting, transaction gating, and lifecycle hooks for cache invalidation.","type":"text"}],"kind":"article"},"doc://LoomCore/documentation/LoomCore/JSONModify":{"url":"\/documentation\/loomcore\/jsonmodify","role":"symbol","title":"JSONModify","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LoomCore\/documentation\/LoomCore\/JSONModify","abstract":[{"text":"SQL ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSON_SET()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSON_INSERT()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" \/ ","type":"text"},{"code":"JSON_REPLACE()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" — a document with edits applied.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"JSONModify","kind":"identifier"}],"kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"JSONModify","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://LoomCore/docume